            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MPEBLE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The taste largely depends on the BBQ sauce you choose. I mixed and let the other ingredients sit overnight to help the flavors blend."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Zombiemom"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great recipe, always a hit with the whole family. I use maple &amp; brown sugar bbq sauce and half the amount of brown sugar you use, and add in a tablespoon or two of spicy brown mustard and mmmm mmm is it delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2013-04-08T13:46:07.567Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Veronica Hardgrave"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used Sweet Baby Ray's and heated all the sauce ingredients in a saucepan. Poured over weenies in crockpot and let in sit overnight. Not sure why I do this but another review did this to a meatball recipe to develop flavors so thought it would be a good idea here too. Heated a few hours before our party. I had a hard time finding 16 oz packages so just used three 14 oz packages and it was still enough sauce but you may have to add a little more ketchup or extra bbq sauce if you have some. They were totally devoured by the end of the night!",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-01T14:00:03.853Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ron"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this but with some slight modifications. I used a \n40oz bottle of Sweet Baby Ray's original bbq sauce,\n20oz bottle of Noh Hawaiian bbq sauce,\n3/4 cup ketchup,\n2 cups brown sugar,\n4tbs Worcestershire sauce,\n2/3 cup minced sweet onion,\n3-4 pkgs of Hillshire Farms Lil smokies .\nThe Noh Hawaiian bbq sauce adds a nice touch of zing.\nI combined all ingredients, except the lil smokies, in a sauce pan and simmered just before boiling so as to let the flavors meld.\nOMG! Is definitely on my favorites list.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-03T16:31:23.093Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ClaU"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Loved it!!!! It's a keeper, you can even add more smokies. I added a little bit of garlic and cayene pepper! Everyone loved them! Thanks for sharing the recipe! I used sweet baby Ray's BBQ sauce! Cooked on crock pot for 4 hours on HIGH because I used double the amount of smokies. The amount of ingredients is enough even of you add twice the amount of smokies. Really good!!",
            "datePublished": "2014-06-28T23:53:42.737Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Debbie Samuels"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was great and easy to make. I too used Sweet Baby Rays sweet 'n' spicy bbq and only a squirt of ketchup and only 3/4 cup of brown sugar. . I'll definitely be using this sauce going forward instead of grape jelly and chili sauce.",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-31T23:53:53.942Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tamara Glover"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I made this for my son's first birthday. It was great. I altered it a bit. I used Kielbasa links cut up into 1 inch rounds and added garlic, hot sauce and red pepper flakes for a kick. The adults at the party absolutely loved them!",
            "datePublished": "2015-12-07T07:11:52.643Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "JoAnn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've always made the recipe with grape jelly. Not any more. The family loved this version. The onion really adds flavor. The next day, we used some of the leftover sauce with smoked pulled pork over rice. Delicious!",
            "datePublished": "2023-02-16T00:18:35.502Z"
          },
